course: dictionary
lesson: 16182
title: An old word: yon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Yon is an old-fashioned word. You will meet it in old poems, fairy tales, older Bible translations and in some dialects, which are ways of speaking used in one place, such as Scotland and the north of England. «Yon hill» means «that hill over there».
explain: Yon can sit in front of a noun, like «yon hill», or be used on its own to mean over there. Context helps: if someone points and says «yon», they mean something further away than «this».
explain: Because yon sounds old and rural, it makes a story feel like it is set long ago or in the countryside. Its close relative yonder means over there too, as in «the yonder hills».
fact: Yon means that, or those, over there.
fact: «Yon hill» means «that hill over there».
fact: Yon can also mean yonder, which is an adverb meaning over there.
fact: «Hither and yon» means here and there, in all directions.
fact: Yon is old-fashioned and dialect, so you will mostly meet it in old texts and in regional speech.
exercise: «We could see yon lighthouse from the boat.» What does yon mean here? | Very tall and thin | Nearby and brand new | *That, over there | Under the sea
exercise: «The sheep wandered hither and yon across the field.» What does hither and yon mean? | Only once | Slowly and carefully | *Here and there, in all directions | Inside the barn
exercise: Which word is a close relative of yon and also means over there? | yesterday | *yonder | yellow | yacht
test: «Yon castle stands on the far side of the river.» What does yon most likely mean? | Broken and empty | *That, over there | Hidden under the water | Very new
test: Grandad pointed at «yon dark wood» and said, «Let's go that way.» Where is yon pointing? | Right next to his feet | Behind the car | *Over there, further away | Inside his pocket
exam: Which sentence uses yon correctly? | *«Look at yon tower on the far hill.» | «Yon is a green colour, like grass.» | «I put yon in the bath every night.» | «Yon cake is a pen for writing.»
